subfinder
Usage: subfinder -d DOMAIN [-silent] [-all]

Passive subdomain discovery. It asks public sources which sub-addresses exist
under a domain -- it sends no packets to the target itself, so it is the
quietest first step of recon. Feed its output to httpx to see which are live.

	-d DOMAIN   the domain to enumerate
	-all        query every source (slower, more complete)
	-silent     just the names, one per line

`example.com` is a reserved name set aside for teaching; real recon is only
for domains you are authorised to assess.

See also: dnsx, httpx, nmap
